{"id":"CVE-2013-4548","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2013-11-08T15:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-06T16:45:15.154Z","description":"The mm_newkeys_from_blob function in monitor_wrap.c in sshd in OpenSSH 6.2 and 6.3, when an AES-GCM cipher is used, does not properly initialize memory for a MAC context data structure, which allows remote authenticated users to bypass intended ForceCommand and login-shell restrictions via packet data that provides a crafted callback address.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.openssh.com/txt/gcmrekey.adv","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2013/11/08/3","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[oss-security] 20131107 Re: CVE Request - OpenSSH"},{"url":"http://marc.info/?l=bugtraq&m=141576985122836&w=2","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_HP"],"name":"HPSBUX03188"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-security-announce/2013-11/msg00017.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2013:1726"},{"url":"http://www.ubuntu.com/usn/USN-2014-1","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-2014-1"}],"vendors":["openssh"]}
